  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14250390/assets/0e3debd878c7c147ce9978bec054fc9d5c9a490bd094060ec1dd3c6ad56ecac9.png)\n\nAn antique broker has records about the value of an artwork $y$ (in thousands of dollars) at certain times $t$ (in decades) since the artwork was produced. The residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on this data set. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $t=5,$ the regression equation underestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data.",
